CORE no-new-smt
main.c
--pointer-check --pointer-overflow-check
^\[main\.pointer_arithmetic\.8\] line \d+ .* in src \+ .*i: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of 20 failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\[main\.pointer_arithmetic\.(9|10)\]
^warning: ignoring
--
The memcpy model wrote its preconditions as `0 || __CPROVER_r_ok(src, n)'
outside the Microsoft runtime.  goto_check_c then checked the instantiated
argument `src + i' again under the guard of the left operand, so each of
these checks was made twice: 22 properties instead of 20.
